            "review_title": "Review at Hutong - Hotpot Paradise",
            "review_text": "emph22\nSingapore, Singapore25 contributions\n0\nNot as outstanding as they may sound\nOct 2018 • Friends\nWe've been to Hutong Le Quy Don on Friday night with a reservation, not so crowded which is good. \n\nStaffs are very attentive and helpful. \n\nWe ordered Lẩu Mala and Lẩu Trường Thọ. I wanted to order Lẩu Cà chua but it's not longer available in the menu, still, it appears in the online menu which is part of the reason I'm there, but nevermind, we chose other options. Mala broth is way too spicy and it does not leave any taste except for its spiciness, and Lẩu trường thọ has almost no taste at all. Or maybe because Mala broth already killed my tongue which I can't taste Lẩu trường thọ at all. Either way, I felt that the broth killed our experience. \n\nThe meat is fresh and nice, we ordered combo beef but the staff suggested us to go for combo pork + beef. The vegetable is nice too. We like the organs, the pig brains and beef marrow. Strongly recommended. \n\nPricing wise, we have 300k VND per person, which is reasonable with their meat quality and ambiance. \n\nOverall, the atmosphere of the restaurant is quite cool and clean, staffs are good, but the food is not that outstanding in my opinion. And I hope they update their online menu for Ho Chi Minh.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten October 8, 2018",
