            "review_text": "Jangtravels\nSingapore, Singapore655 contributions\n0\nGreat hotpot place\nDec 2017 • Family\nThe restaurant is located near the war remnant museum and makes for a good eating spot before or after a visit to the museum. \n\nThe ambience is great and very Chinese - which add flavour to the meal. You can order a single pot or a split pot (which means you can taste 2 types of soup base in the same pot). \n\nOrdering is simple as the menu has pictures. They have English speaking staff as well who would gladly assist.\n\nYou order by dishes - vegetable, mushrooms, fish, chicken, beef, pork. Make sure you try the home made noodle they make in the shop. Try ordering the iced tea - very refreshing.\n\nThere are clean toilets and free wifi as well. Enjoy!\nRead more\nWritten December 23, 2017",
